# BreezeLink Edge AI — the App Lab build (runs on the Arduino UNO Q).
#
#   copy to .env and fill it in:   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env IS GITIGNORED and build-applab-app.py DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DELETE IT (it only
# rebuilds edge_ai/ and app/). It holds the household's ORG_ID — something with no other
# copy to restore from if lost.
#
# THERE ARE NO MQTT CREDENTIALS HERE, and that is the crucial point: this service talks
# to the gateway over UART, not through a broker. That is exactly why it survives the
# network outage it was built to survive.

# =============================================================================
#  REQUIRED
# =============================================================================
# From the admin web -> Khách hàng -> open the "Gateway trong nhà" node ->
# "Nạp firmware".
#
# This value is HASHED into the `link_key` the gateway checks on every packet. With the
# wrong ORG_ID the gateway silently refuses every command: ITS log records "rejected
# packet with wrong link_key", while this node's log records NOTHING AT ALL — it sent
# successfully, the other end simply discarded it. The only symptom is "the air
# conditioner does not move".
EDGE_ORG_ID=

# =============================================================================
#  THE PATH TO THE GATEWAY
# =============================================================================
# auto (default) | bridge | serial
#
#   bridge  through the sketch on the STM32 half out to pins D0/D1  <- CORRECT for App Lab
#   serial  through the Linux half's USB-TTL port
#
# "auto" probes whether /var/run/arduino-router.sock exists. Inside App Lab it always
# picks bridge, so there is usually NOTHING TO FILL IN.
#
# THESE TWO CANNOT BOTH BE RIGHT — the cable only plugs into one place. Wired to D0/D1
# but forced to serial, pyserial grabs some other port at random and then waits forever,
# and the symptom ("no snapshots") looks exactly like a broken cable.
# EDGE_LINK=auto

# Only used when EDGE_LINK=serial. Leave empty to auto-detect (preferring
# CH34x/CP210x/FTDI bridge chips). Declare it by hand when the UART pins are wired
# directly: Linux cannot guess which /dev/ttyS* is connected to what.
# EDGE_UART_PORT=/dev/ttyUSB0

# =============================================================================
#  LEARNED IR CODES — worth filling in, see the trap below
# =============================================================================
# The temperatures this household HAS LEARNED IR CODES for in COOL mode.
#
# It has to be declared by hand because the edge node has no path to Postgres — the
# `ir_codes` table lives on the server, and the entire reason this node exists is to
# keep running when the server is gone.
#
# Get the real list with:
#     SELECT DISTINCT temp FROM ir_codes WHERE mode='COOL' ORDER BY temp;
#
# LEAVING IT EMPTY IS NOT THE SAFE OPTION. The node then learns by watching the server
# issue commands, and right after startup it has seen exactly ONE level (say 27).
# nearest_captured_temp() always returns the nearest level in the list it currently
# has — so a target of 24.5 is forced to 27, with no error and no warning. A half-filled
# list is MORE DANGEROUS than an empty one: an empty one makes NoIrCodesError stop
# everything.
# EDGE_IR_TEMPS=24,25,26,27,28

# =============================================================================
#  WEATHER FORECAST (open-meteo, no API key needed)
# =============================================================================
# The installation site's coordinates. BOTH must be present or both left empty —
# declaring only one is a configuration error rather than "disabled", because it is
# almost certainly a typo.
#
# Left empty the thermal model still runs, but looking further ahead than ~15 minutes it
# has to assume the outdoor temperature stands still.
# EDGE_LAT=10.701285
# EDGE_LON=106.625595

# =============================================================================
#  AUTHORITY TO COMMAND
# =============================================================================
# 1/true/yes = ADVICE ONLY, never command — even when the cloud is gone.
#
# Enable it during a trial run to compare the edge's decisions against the server's
# BEFORE handing it real authority. Only turn it off once the monitoring page (port
# 7000) reports the forecast as TRUSTWORTHY.
EDGE_ADVISORY_ONLY=1

# How long the server has to be silent before the UNO Q takes control (seconds).
# 300 is deliberately generous: both sides commanding means the air conditioner
# receives two contradictory orders within the same minute, and the symptom (a setpoint
# that jumps on its own) looks exactly like an algorithm bug. Better to take over late.
# EDGE_TAKEOVER_AFTER_SEC=300

# =============================================================================
#  LOCAL HISTORY (SQLite) — the foundation of the thermal model
# =============================================================================
# Without it, every service restart puts the model back to zero and it takes about 10
# hours to become usable again.
#
# LEAVING IT EMPTY IS CORRECT. The default is data/ next to the edge_ai package, i.e.
# inside the app directory — the ONLY place in App Lab that is both writable and
# survives a container rebuild. Every other path vanishes with the container.
# EDGE_HISTORY_DB=
# EDGE_HISTORY_DAYS=30

# =============================================================================
#  TUNING — rarely needs touching
# =============================================================================
# THIS household's algorithm configuration, pasted from the "Cấu hình thuật toán" page.
# LEAVING IT EMPTY USES THE DEFAULTS — and if the household has been tuned on the web,
# the edge will compute a setpoint DIFFERENT from the server's, with neither side
# reporting an error.
# EDGE_COMFORT_CONFIG={"ema_alpha":0.2,"deadband":0.8,"dwell_sec":600,"dry_rh":72,"humid_slope":0.05,"clamp_min":24,"clamp_max":28,"override_hours":2,"night_start":23,"night_end":6,"night_offset":0.5}

# The sliding window of per-corner readings (seconds). Long enough for the regression to
# have something to hold on to, short enough that an afternoon of harsh sun is not
# diluted by a cool morning.
# EDGE_HISTORY_SEC=1800

# The control loop interval (seconds). It does not need to be short: room temperature
# does not change over 30 seconds, and every iteration can emit an IR command.
# EDGE_TICK_SEC=30

# EDGE_RECONNECT_SEC=5
# EDGE_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# EDGE_BACKEND_SRC IS NOT NEEDED in the App Lab build: build-applab-app.py already ships
# the app/comfort/ slice right next to edge_ai/, so `app.comfort` imports directly. That
# variable is only for the systemd build (see ../../../../.env.example).
